From 6f561752b719c94f6051bc6257515e4729edf110 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Reixo <125610085+Reixo0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 16:20:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu, panel: rm692h5: switch refresh rates without a
 modeset

A command mode DSI panel paces itself, so a mode that keeps the size,
line length and pixel clock and only changes the vertical blanking
keeps the DSI link timing. Such a change no longer needs a modeset:

- drm_panel gets an optional switch_mode op, reachable through the
  panel bridge, that moves a lit panel to another refresh rate.
- dpu: crtc atomic_check clears mode_changed for a lit crtc whose
  command mode DSI encoders end in such a panel and whose new mode
  differs only in its refresh rate. At the next kickoff, after the
  previous frame is out, the encoder hands the panel the new mode and
  reprograms the tear check for it.
- rm692h5: all four rates (60/90/120/144 Hz) keep the 144 Hz link and
  get a longer vertical front porch instead; switch_mode sends the
  rate's register set in HS mode, under a lock shared with brightness
  updates (both write paged registers).

A rate change used to turn the panel off and on (a black frame); now it
takes one frame and ~3-7 ms of register writes, with nothing visible.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
